  "body": "Somehow we've never specified `unsigned.prev_sender` - a field on state events which tells you who the sender was of the state event that was replaced by the current state event.\n\nAs far as I can see, what happened is:\n * @richvdh first specced it in 2015 for CS events: 29bd4d45ee9155bd80e61ce50ab34745be1fd8a4 and 6653362f315d1379d1dda248dfd299c8c3c8530d\n * @turt2live then moved it to a SS-specific `unsigned` block in 2018: 5027a9a59a4ca257f6b71f78f6f0fe3811940400\n * @richvdh then removed it from the SS block in [#3522](https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/3522)\n * `prev_content` got re-specced based in [#3524](https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/3524) based on https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/issues/877\n * `replaces_state` eventually got re-specced a few months ago thanks to @timedoutuk in https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec/pull/2345 closing https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec/issues/274\n\n...but somehow `prev_sender` got missed from all this (which confuses me greatly: isn't it in the same bucket as `replaces_state`?).\n\nIn practice, `prev_sender` is in use in the wild:\n * matrix-js-sdk uses it to determine DMedness of things\n * matrix-js-sdk also uses it to 'play state backwards' for sync v2\n * It's also useful for seeing who answered a knock\n * Synapse implements it\n * Continuwuity (picking an indie server at random) implements it too\n\nTherefore, surely it should be specced as an omission?",
